        "math_academy_id": "q-182498",
        "problem": "Simplify the statement $\u00ac(R\u21d2\u00acS).$",
        "worked_solution": "The conditional statement $P\u21d2Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $\u00acP\u2228Q:$\n\nSo, in this case, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n\u00ac(R\u21d2\u00acS)\u2261\u00ac(\u00acR\u2228\u00acS)\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u00acR\u2228\u00acS)\u2261\u00ac(\u00acR)\u2227\u00ac(\u00acS).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nR\u2227S.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $R\u2227S.$",
